## Week 3 — Implementation of New Feature Engineering Pipeline

- Implemented the Graph Attention Engine: replaced the static Laplacian residual module with an attention-weighted graph aggregation that adapts to the current correlation structure without a fixed threshold.
- Implemented adaptive percentile-based thresholding as a preprocessing step: the correlation graph threshold is set at the 70th percentile of observed pairwise correlations in each rolling window, making graph density consistent across regimes.
- Implemented the Walsh-Hadamard spectral scorer: at each time step, computes the spectral decomposition of the binary return vector across the stock universe and returns a scalar synchronisation score.
- Implemented the Persistent Homology extractor using the Ripser library: extracts H0 and H1 persistence diagrams from the stock correlation distance matrix, then summarises them as entropy and beta-stability scalars.
- Implemented the regime classifier: uses rolling volatility percentile and index drawdown to assign one of four market regimes per day, encoded as a 4-dimensional one-hot vector.
- Merged all 16 channels into a unified feature DataFrame per ticker and verified output shapes — each stock produces a (T × 16) feature matrix, windowed into (N × 16 × 64) tensors for model input.
- Verified feature correctness by inspecting feature values during known historical events: confirmed that H0 persistence spikes during IL&FS crisis (September 2018) and COVID crash (March 2020), validating that topological features correctly detect market fragmentation.
- Ran the data preparation pipeline on the NSE dataset (49 Nifty-50 tickers, 2010–2021) and confirmed successful feature generation for all tickers.

