## Week 5 — Evaluation, Statistical Validation & Portfolio Analysis

- Conducted a comprehensive statistical significance analysis on prediction quality:
  - Per-window binomial tests with Wilson 95% confidence intervals across all five test windows (W3–W7).
  - Model achieved individual significance in the Elections/Slowdown window (p = 0.0075, hit rate = 52.13%).
  - Pooled binomial test across 25,862 confident predictions: hit rate = 50.67%, Z-score = 2.14, p = 0.033 — statistically significant at the 5% level.
  - Paired t-tests vs all 10 baselines (n = 5 window pairs): model significantly outperforms Momentum-5 (p = 0.0016, Cohen's d = 3.4), MACD Crossover (p = 0.012), and Momentum-1 (p = 0.021).
  - Model is statistically at parity with the well-trained 7-channel TCN (p = 0.73, gap = 0.18 pp), indicating that the flat TCN architecture does not fully exploit the richer 16-channel topological feature set.
- Performed NSE-realistic portfolio transaction cost analysis:
  - Calculated break-even hit rate at discount broker rates (Zerodha-class, round-trip ≈ 0.208%): break-even threshold = 50.10%.
  - Confirmed that the model's pooled hit rate (50.67%) exceeds this break-even by +0.57 pp, establishing that the strategy is technically profitable after real Indian market transaction costs.
  - At institutional-grade costs (round-trip ≈ 0.05%), break-even drops to 50.03% — well below the model's performance.
- Documented the confident prediction deadband: trades are executed only when model output probability exceeds 0.55 (long) or falls below 0.45 (short), filtering out low-conviction signals and focusing evaluation on high-confidence predictions.
- Identified the primary architectural limitation for future work: a flat TCN applies identical convolutional filters to both sequential momentum features (RSI, MACD) and instantaneous structural features (GAT signal, H0, H1), which is architecturally suboptimal. Proposed a dual-branch TCN and channel attention mechanism (Squeeze-and-Excitation) as the natural next improvements.
- Compiled all results — per-window hit rates, significance test outcomes, transaction cost analysis, and regime-specific performance breakdown — into the final project report.
